Web Application Firewall publishes sites through the firewall: each
request to a site is received on the firewall by an Apache of the
plugin's own, inspected by ModSecurity 2.9 with the OWASP Core Rule Set
(the 4.25 line), and passed to the site's backend over HTTP or HTTPS.
Each site has its host names, its certificate of System: Trust or none,
its paranoia level from 1 to 4, and its mode: Detection only, where
what the rules find is logged and the request passes - every new site's
first mode - or Blocking, where an attack is refused with 403. The
audit log is kept in JSON, a file a day. The Core Rule Set is installed
from a release this project republished signed, once the Core Rule
Set's own signature was checked. Apache and ModSecurity are OPNsense's
own packages, apache24 and ap24-mod_security. Off by default; a port
the web GUI listens on is refused, never taken. It adds no firewall
rule.

